# {{ .name }}

An Intropy loader. It consumes the `{{ .subscribes }}` message from the
system's pub/sub (topic `{{ .channel }}`), runs each event through a loader
pipeline (deserialize, validate, idempotency check, transform, send) and
writes the result through the `{{ .port }}` destination port. It is a
long-running worker; in production it runs as a Deployment.
{{- if .empty }}

The pipeline steps were scaffolded empty: each throws
`NotImplementedException` until it is implemented.
{{- end }}

## Build and test

```bash
task build
task test
```

The loader does not run standalone. Run it with the rest of the system from
the system host (`task run` there).

## Container image

```bash
docker build --build-context contracts=../{{ .contracts }} -t {{ .appId }} .
```

See `AGENTS.md` for the component's names, ports and key files, and
<https://docs.intropy.io> for how loaders work.
